# L §8.3 item 10 (round 19, GD-4): "The random cone (step 10): every item that reaches a dist fact through the item graph,
# in each world, and through every place a random movement books into: a balance or a projection of such a place is in
# the cone, so a line that reads it without a query is refused at load, as any random line is (LOAD-RANDOM, §5.16)";
# E §3.1 step 10. buy (amount round(spend[m]), a dist) books konto. low(konto, span) on an ask line: a balance of konto, refused at load.
=== m.tally
model r
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind spends: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input spend_mu: money PLN
input spend_sd: money PLN
input spend_dom: int
def spend[m in months]: dist PLN = normal(spend_mu, spend_sd) to 1e-9 at end_of(m)

move buy[m in months]: spends
  on day_of(m, spend_dom)
  at end_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to shop amount round(spend[m], minor(PLN), half-even)

version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  spend_mu = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  spend_sd = 100.00 PLN "own"
  spend_dom = 15 "own"
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"

ask l1: low(konto, 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-RANDOM ask l1: low(konto, 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-31) is random; apply a query (m.tally:32)
